NAME
    mv - move or rename files and directories (currently suspended)

SYNOPSIS
    mv <src> <dst>

SUSPENDED
    mv currently refuses all invocations and exits with status 1. It was
    parked when the shell sandbox still encompassed install binaries;
    although '/' is now rooted at EmuSen's home directory (see hier(7)),
    the safeguard remains in place. The section below describes the
    command's intended interface.

DESCRIPTION
    Moves or renames a file or directory within the shell sandbox. If
    <dst> is an existing directory, <src> is moved inside it under its
    base name. An existing destination file is overwritten without
    prompting.

EXAMPLES
    mv /Logs/scratch.txt /Logs/archive/

EXIT STATUS
    1   Always fails while suspended.

SEE ALSO
    cp(1), rm(1), hier(7)
